<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Friday 101,000-USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Friday 101,000-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Friday's actual interior Iowa/southern Minnesota hog receipts were 101,000 head, compared with the estimate of 100,000, USDA said.  Saturday's receipts were 11,000 head, compared with the estimate of 15,000. Opening trade not well established.  Early sales Barrows and Gilts $0.50 higher compared to midsession Friday.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    56.50 -57.50	   57.50 -58.50</p>
<p>			   56.00  58.00	   57.00 -59.00</p>
<p>Sows: steady to $1.50 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  44.00 -46.00	   44.00 -48.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   45.00 -49.00	   45.00 -49.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -53.00	   48.00 -54.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
